Fixed. The bug was in `src/import_merge.ts:7` — the duplicate check compared full URLs with `===`, which is case-sensitive, so `https://example.com/a` and `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` never matched.

**Change:** comparison now uses a `safeHost` helper that lowercases each URL's hostname (parsed via `URL`), so differing hostname casing is treated as the same URL. Unparseable URLs fall back to `""` and simply won't match anything (safe default — they'd be appended rather than merged).

Verified: `deno lint` clean, all 3 existing tests pass. No existing test covered `mergeImports`; I left the fixture untouched per the isolation rules.


